1
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:40,666
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

2
00:00:48,674 --> 00:00:51,385
Don't you think
Prince Heinrey is so dashing?

3
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:23,875
Your Highness, I heard
that you've searched ardently.

4
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:27,254
I am the secret pen pal
you've been writing to.

5
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:31,341
Your "lost fate", and you found me now.

6
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:06,793
So, you say…

7
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:08,878
you're my correspondent?

8
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:10,464
Yes.

9
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:14,676
Prove it to me.

10
00:02:18,597 --> 00:02:20,641
You're suspicious, aren't you?

11
00:02:22,017 --> 00:02:24,143
Yes, with good reason too.

12
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:26,605
This is someone
who is very precious to me.

13
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:33,362
If you really are that person,
I would be happy.

14
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:36,531
But if you are not that person,

15
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:39,868
there would be consequences
for disappointing me.

16
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:42,704
What exactly might you do?

17
00:02:47,751 --> 00:02:48,752
Who can say?

18
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,338
Do not think about that.

19
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:54,257
That will never occur with us in any case.

20
00:02:57,344 --> 00:03:00,012
Since I shall prove to you
that I was indeed

21
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:01,598
behind those letters.

22
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:06,352
Only we know the bird is our messenger.

23
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:07,646
That is a secret.

24
00:03:09,064 --> 00:03:10,482
It is only me

25
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:12,692
and you, the prince,

26
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:14,361
who know the bird has a name.

27
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:16,613
What is the bird's name?

28
00:03:18,657 --> 00:03:19,658
It is Queen.

29
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:23,536
That bird's noble feathers appealed to me,

30
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:26,247
so Rashta was the one
who personally named it.

31
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:27,541
Queen.

32
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,095
The name is correct.

33
00:03:41,972 --> 00:03:43,055
Queen.

34
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:13,085
Where is Queen now?

35
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:15,755
I'm sure he's near you.

36
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:21,595
Queen! Where are you?

37
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:23,889
Come out and see us!

38
00:04:24,431 --> 00:04:26,474
<i>Rashta is here!</i>

39
00:04:26,475 --> 00:04:28,268
Come on out here!

40
00:04:29,144 --> 00:04:30,478
Queen!

41
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:31,730
Where are you?

42
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:34,274
Come out and see me!

43
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:44,950
I did not wish to offend.
I had to confirm it was you.

44
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:47,496
You were seeking someone
who's very dear to you.

45
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:53,918
It took much courage for Rashta,
who is the Emperor's woman,

46
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:56,296
to seek you out
while everyone is watching.

47
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:00,133
I've waited for this.

48
00:05:02,427 --> 00:05:04,137
I wanted very much for us to meet.

49
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:26,075
That sly fox. She has no shame, does she?

50
00:05:26,076 --> 00:05:27,451
It's that Rashta again.

51
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:28,702
She's claiming that she's the one

52
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:31,248
who is exchanging secret letters
with Prince Heinrey.

53
00:05:32,082 --> 00:05:33,165
Oh goodness.

54
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:35,709
Your Majesty, only you can put this right.

55
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:38,504
You should expose her lies
and humiliate her so thoroughly

56
00:05:38,505 --> 00:05:40,923
that she won't be able
to show her face again.

57
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:44,636
There's more to this.

58
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:48,765
The content of those letters
was private and personal.

59
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:52,853
So how could Rashta know it?

60
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:02,862
My apologies.

61
00:06:02,863 --> 00:06:04,780
I will bring the source to light

62
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:06,490
and punish the spy.

63
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:08,118
I shall restore discipline, my lady.

64
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:13,123
Ah!

65
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:15,291
-  This way!
- Where are you?

66
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:16,625
- Where?
- I'm here!

67
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,837
-  Here?
-  Here, over here!

68
00:06:19,421 --> 00:06:21,213
- Go on, yes!
-  Where are you?

69
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:22,423
Aw! He moved!

70
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:24,550
-  Quick, she's coming for us!
- Where are you? Here?

71
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:27,804
Oh! Oh.

72
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,681
Oh.

73
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:32,225
Are you hurt?

74
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:34,352
Your hand.

75
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,107
There! I beat you!

76
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:42,484
Get up.

77
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,987
Here, I'll help you.

78
00:06:44,988 --> 00:06:46,531
I beat you!

79
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:48,699
I caught you.

80
00:06:51,578 --> 00:06:53,621
-  Where are you going?
-  Come over here!

81
00:06:53,622 --> 00:06:55,456
Come around it! Come this way!

82
00:06:55,457 --> 00:06:56,957
Careful!

83
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:59,168
"I beat you."

84
00:06:59,169 --> 00:07:00,669
-  This way!
-  Here we are!

85
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:01,920
Go on, get her!

86
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:10,387
How's this?

87
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:11,847
You'd look so beautiful,
as always.

88
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,725
Ms. Rashta!

89
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:18,229
Just look how many invitations
people have sent you!

90
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,943
I think everyone
is talking about you today.

91
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:27,571
They are all saying
that there's no competition,

92
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:29,990
and there's no one
as dazzling as you this New Year!

93
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:33,702
Our banquet needs a larger venue.
Don't you think?

94
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:34,787
Absolutely.

95
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:36,664
More than 100 people will come.

96
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:38,500
Well, I must tell Lady Albani, then.

97
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:41,919
Throw these away.

98
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,296
They're just petty gatherings.

99
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:46,674
I'll be far too busy
with all the important parties.

100
00:07:46,675 --> 00:07:47,925
Of course.

101
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:48,927
Ah.

102
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:51,845
Can you please tell us
about Prince Heinrey?

103
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:54,431
- He seems lovely.
- You two look so wonderful together.

104
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:56,392
- It's true!
- Really?

105
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:58,186
Given what's happened…

106
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,356
I think you should take him as a lover.

107
00:08:02,691 --> 00:08:06,569
Can the Emperor's lady
make a conquest of her own?

108
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:10,239
More to the point, who would know?

109
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:20,207
What should we do with the present
that came with the invitation?

110
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,459
A present, you say?

111
00:08:24,796 --> 00:08:27,089
-  Ta-da!
-  It's a beautiful carpet!

112
00:08:28,258 --> 00:08:29,509
But where are the jewels?

113
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,760
It looks expensive.

114
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:34,389
And a real high-quality item
for sure.

115
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:37,391
- You have it.
- Mmm. Me?

116
00:08:37,392 --> 00:08:41,437
I would say you deserve a reward
for all your hard work with the letters.

117
00:08:41,438 --> 00:08:42,771
Oh!

118
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:44,440
Thank you, Ms. Rashta, truly!

119
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:46,025
In return,

120
00:08:46,026 --> 00:08:47,819
you must find out even more now.

121
00:08:48,403 --> 00:08:50,237
I want to know everything that's written.

122
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:53,323
Also, bring any information
on the Empress' life.

123
00:08:53,324 --> 00:08:54,701
But stay discreet.

124
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:58,370
Kisia, the same goes for you.

125
00:08:58,371 --> 00:08:59,664
Hear this.

126
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:02,791
Stay faithful to me.

127
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:05,335
I'll be even more generous
if you stay loyal.

128
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:06,795
Yes, I will, Ms. Rashta.

129
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,216
Majesty!

130
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:17,724
Mmm. I missed you so much.

131
00:09:18,475 --> 00:09:21,102
You have something to say?

132
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:25,607
You've been listening to the rumors, then?
Have you?

133
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:30,736
I tried to tell you about it first,
Your Majesty.

134
00:09:30,737 --> 00:09:33,364
I did go to your palace yesterday.

135
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,158
And again this morning.

136
00:09:38,912 --> 00:09:42,916
Everyone in the palace prefers talking
to Her Majesty the Empress.

137
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,501
Rashta was feeling lonely.

138
00:09:45,502 --> 00:09:48,504
Nobody wants anything to do with Rashta.

139
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:50,089
I just wanted a friend.

140
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:52,175
It was nice even just by letter.

141
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:57,346
With a foreign royal?

142
00:09:57,347 --> 00:10:00,182
But I would have preferred it
much, much more

143
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:01,351
to spend time with you.

144
00:10:04,813 --> 00:10:06,313
Well, then,

145
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:09,399
did those blasted letters
bring you some comfort

146
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,069
in your lonely palace life?

147
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:13,195
You're all I need.

148
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:14,823
My comfort is you, Your Majesty.

149
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:19,576
Your Majesty is my sunshine

150
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:20,787
and my big joy…

151
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:22,831
and salvation.

152
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,292
Oh!

153
00:10:28,378 --> 00:10:29,587
Cute.

154
00:10:31,131 --> 00:10:32,132
Cute as can be.

155
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:35,301
You're even more cute when you're sulking.

156
00:10:35,927 --> 00:10:38,012
Cute when you're being jealous.

157
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:41,431
The cutest man.

158
00:10:41,432 --> 00:10:43,559
Rashta has one request.

159
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:45,979
I have heard
there's another banquet arranged.

160
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,438
Rashta would like you
to bring her, please.

161
00:10:48,439 --> 00:10:49,731
Since this one is special,

162
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:52,235
and all the most important people
will be there.

163
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:54,027
If you know all of that,

164
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:56,405
then you should also know
that you're not allowed to attend.

165
00:10:56,406 --> 00:10:58,031
If you take me,

166
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:00,951
I won't be forced to ask Prince Heinrey
to take me instead.

167
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:03,955
Aw!

168
00:11:05,123 --> 00:11:06,791
Please take me with you. Mm.

169
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:13,213
They are calling it
"The rediscovery of Ms. Rashta."

170
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:14,882
Her commoner-like cheerfulness.

171
00:11:14,883 --> 00:11:17,594
And, of course, the praise for her looks
goes without saying!

172
00:11:18,303 --> 00:11:19,678
What else did they say?

173
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:23,432
"She's as innocent as a baby
and a total angel."

174
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:25,560
Ha! What a joke.

175
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:30,439
So, why on earth
are you letting her fool you?

176
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:31,565
What is it?

177
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:33,483
Why are you doing this?

178
00:11:33,484 --> 00:11:35,777
Her blatant lies
haven't pushed you over the edge?

179
00:11:35,778 --> 00:11:37,738
It's party to party with her on your arm.

180
00:11:37,739 --> 00:11:41,158
Why are you escorting her around
and raising her value like that?

181
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:43,911
- Her happiness, that's why.
- What?

182
00:11:43,912 --> 00:11:46,998
I'll indulge her and let her prance around
to her heart's content.

183
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:52,420
Then my next move,
when she is perfectly at ease…

184
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,431
You are such a sly, devious person.

185
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:05,642
Are you aware of that?

186
00:12:06,768 --> 00:12:08,602
I very clearly warned that woman.

187
00:12:08,603 --> 00:12:10,187
Enough is enough.

188
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:12,940
I told her if she lied,
my anger would be severe.

189
00:12:12,941 --> 00:12:14,567
She has to pay the price.

190
00:12:17,779 --> 00:12:19,238
The price

191
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:21,491
for exploiting a prince
to grow her status.

192
00:12:24,786 --> 00:12:25,912
The price…

193
00:12:26,371 --> 00:12:28,456
for daring to act the "Queen".

194
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:38,215
What is the order of entrance?

195
00:12:38,216 --> 00:12:39,758
Grand Duke Kaufman of Luipt,

196
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:42,469
Princess Circe,
Prince Heinrey of the Western Kingdom,

197
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,304
then Grand Prince Sirim of Bohemia.

198
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:46,056
The Grand Duke will be in blue-green,

199
00:12:46,057 --> 00:12:48,141
Prince Heinrey will be dressed in white,

200
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:50,143
and Emperor Sovieshu in black.

201
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:53,189
Shall we prepare black for you as well,
to match His Majesty?

202
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:58,861
Could I select something for you to wear?

203
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:02,490
Simple and elegant.

204
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:35,315
Her Majesty the Empress,
Navier Ellie Trovi, is entering.

205
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:44,322
The bird was just so lovely,
and that's why I named it Queen.

206
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,242
Really?

207
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,201
Sist…

208
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,203
Ah.

209
00:13:50,413 --> 00:13:52,248
Your Majesty.

210
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:04,385
Your Majesty, you've come at last.

211
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:14,019
"Sister"?

212
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,063
Uh…

213
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:17,773
You know what I really think?

214
00:14:17,774 --> 00:14:20,358
She's far too old to be my big sister.

215
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:26,491
It's an honor to be seated next to you,
Your Majesty.

216
00:14:30,912 --> 00:14:32,370
Were you surprised?

217
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:34,414
Actually, I'm impressed.

218
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:37,042
I had thought I would be the most stylish…

219
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:38,878
and then I saw you, Princess Circe.

220
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:43,590
I'm afraid Grand Duke Kaufman
won't even meet my eyes

221
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:45,258
because of what I'm wearing.

222
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:49,262
In Luipt, it is considered extremely rude
for a lady to wear trousers.

223
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:51,723
It's seen to be
an act of great disrespect.

224
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:53,266
I wear trousers when hunting.

225
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:54,392
They're comfortable.

226
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:56,561
Customs vary between kingdoms.

227
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,063
What on earth is wisteria?

228
00:15:01,818 --> 00:15:04,778
In my country,
if a man's lover ever approached his wife,

229
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:06,905
she would be executed immediately.

230
00:15:26,717 --> 00:15:29,803
Ms. Rashta's new necklace
is perfectly beautiful.

231
00:15:29,804 --> 00:15:33,015
I heard it was a gift
from you, Your Majesty.

232
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:35,268
Really?

233
00:15:37,979 --> 00:15:40,564
Yes. Ms. Rashta told us so.

234
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:43,651
That you sent it as a gift
to mark her entering the palace.

235
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:47,655
That Your Majesty cares for
and cherishes her like family.

236
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,076
She's mistaken.

237
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:54,995
I did not send her anything.

238
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:56,955
- Ms. Rashta is confused.
- Ah…

239
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:58,748
This is surely a misunderstanding.

240
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:00,500
Are you sure you are my pen pal?

241
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:02,752
- I hope you are not lying to me.
- Yes, a misunderstanding.

242
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,172
What do you mean, lying?

243
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:10,218
Prince Heinrey, why such rudeness?

244
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:11,636
I don't believe I'm rude.

245
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:14,055
It is Rashta who has been rude.

246
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:16,684
I told you to be careful with your words.

247
00:16:17,727 --> 00:16:20,729
Your mistress
should be equally careful with hers.

248
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:22,105
Mistress?

249
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,649
Mistress?

250
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:30,448
Rashta did plainly tell you
she was a little lost.

251
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:34,827
Might she not have just forgotten
a trivial letter?

252
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:38,121
Heinrey explained it to her plainly.

253
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:40,332
One could forget a letter's contents,

254
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:43,085
but one cannot forget the very town
they were born in.

255
00:16:47,215 --> 00:16:48,590
Everyone!

256
00:16:48,591 --> 00:16:52,052
Ms. Rashta claimed she was the one
who exchanged letters with me,

257
00:16:52,053 --> 00:16:53,471
and I believed it was true.

258
00:16:54,222 --> 00:16:56,806
After all, a woman
who is loved by His Majesty

259
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:59,227
surely possesses a character
worthy of that love.

260
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:01,353
I believed she was trustworthy.

261
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:04,814
Today, I wanted to speak to her
about their contents,

262
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:06,275
so we discussed them.

263
00:17:07,735 --> 00:17:09,737
And my letters were not written by her.

264
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,201
A fake.

265
00:17:17,954 --> 00:17:19,371
That's enough now.

266
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:20,373
Stop, Prince Heinrey.

267
00:17:20,957 --> 00:17:21,958
Ah…

268
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:24,834
I would have settled this quietly.

269
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:27,045
Your Majesty chose not to keep it private.

270
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:30,257
Is it not considered chivalrous
to defend your woman,

271
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:32,133
more so when she's defenseless?

272
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:34,135
If the chivalry of the Western Kingdom

273
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:37,430
means treating a young woman so harshly
over some letters

274
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:38,974
that don't even matter…

275
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:40,725
I wouldn't say any more on this.

276
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:45,772
I, too, want to defend a young lady
who has been unfairly misused.

277
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:48,859
Although, of course, the one
being impersonated may not be a woman,

278
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:52,488
I might even be a man.

279
00:17:56,909 --> 00:18:00,413
How can you be so cruel?
Rashta has never been a fake.

280
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:03,665
What would be the reason for me to lie?

281
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:05,542
It's Heinrey who won't leave it alone.

282
00:18:05,543 --> 00:18:08,170
He's trying to twist things
so I look like a liar.

283
00:18:09,797 --> 00:18:12,173
Well, I think I've worked out
why you're doing this.

284
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,175
I think it's…

285
00:18:14,051 --> 00:18:16,177
because Rashta's not a highborn lady.

286
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,888
Not refined, like you wanted.

287
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:21,016
So you're deliberately
distancing yourself.

288
00:18:21,017 --> 00:18:24,145
Was the friendship that you showed Rashta
until this point all a lie?

289
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:26,188
Is that true?

290
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:36,991
Ms. Rashta…

291
00:18:43,706 --> 00:18:46,541
out of the countless people
I have come across,

292
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:48,544
you're by far the most brazen.

293
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:53,798
I ask you, for the sake of our friendship,

294
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:55,425
don't say such things, please.

295
00:18:55,426 --> 00:18:57,511
They hurt Rashta!

296
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:15,029
I planned to remain silent.

297
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:19,116
Misunderstandings have arisen.

298
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:21,577
So I believe I must set them right.

299
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:23,746
Your Majesty…

300
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:29,959
I happen to know
who wrote Prince Heinrey those letters.

301
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,587
I know with whom he corresponds.

302
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:38,594
Rashta is not that person.

303
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,730
None of this is your concern.

304
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:52,400
Just because you dislike Rashta,

305
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:56,237
you don't need to support the prince
or become involved.

306
00:19:56,821 --> 00:19:59,155
The truth must always be respected.

307
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:02,325
It seems that Ms. Rashta
can only speak the truth

308
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:04,704
according to His Majesty the Emperor.

309
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:12,961
It must be maddening, Your Majesty.

310
00:20:12,962 --> 00:20:13,963
What a pity.

311
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:37,819
You've pushed this too far.

312
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:04,722
So, Heinrey…

313
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:08,350
for tainting my lady's reputation…

314
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:12,021
I challenge you to a duel.

315
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:15,816
A duel?

316
00:21:21,071 --> 00:21:22,155
Ma… Majesty!

317
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:25,367
Get out! Get out, quickly!
Move it! Get out of here!

318
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:34,876
Shoo! Get out, now!

319
00:21:34,877 --> 00:21:36,420
I said get out!

320
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:53,604
If I did manage to kill you,

321
00:21:54,522 --> 00:21:56,023
would I get out of here alive?

322
00:22:15,918 --> 00:22:19,171
If I would walk free, then I accept.

323
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:21,882
Too much talk.

324
00:22:46,657 --> 00:22:48,033
Oh no!

325
00:24:12,034 --> 00:24:13,451
You're just like children.

326
00:24:13,452 --> 00:24:14,787
It's absurd!

327
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:17,456
Do you think this behavior is justified?

328
00:24:20,918 --> 00:24:22,294
A duel?

329
00:24:24,004 --> 00:24:25,589
Oh, how foolish you must be.

330
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:29,342
If either of you were to be killed,

331
00:24:29,343 --> 00:24:31,095
a great war would begin.

332
00:24:32,638 --> 00:24:35,391
Imagine… the pain and suffering
it would cause.

333
00:24:35,975 --> 00:24:37,475
Thousands of your subjects' lives

334
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:39,770
hang in the balance
between men and their swordplay.

335
00:24:43,399 --> 00:24:45,192
Is your pride worth so much?

336
00:24:48,821 --> 00:24:50,489
Please do not forget yourself.

337
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:53,783
I know your correspondent
would not approve.

338
00:24:53,784 --> 00:24:55,452
For the sake of that friendship…

339
00:24:56,245 --> 00:24:57,246
stop this.

340
00:25:12,970 --> 00:25:14,763
It has been a memorable evening.

341
00:25:17,891 --> 00:25:20,394
I hope there's time tomorrow
for us to speak again.

342
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:23,856
So do I.
I'll find a good time for us to meet.

343
00:25:28,110 --> 00:25:30,028
The most joyous aspect of this year,

344
00:25:30,029 --> 00:25:31,529
aside from the celebrations,

345
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:33,114
is finding you, Princess.

346
00:25:33,115 --> 00:25:35,992
I agree.
It looks as though we think alike.

347
00:25:35,993 --> 00:25:37,661
Here's to friendship, then.

348
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:44,668
Do come back and have fun
with Rashta again tomorrow.

349
00:25:56,889 --> 00:25:59,433
I will just wait here
so I can return with His Majesty.

350
00:26:07,858 --> 00:26:08,859
Rashta.

351
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:10,903
Yes?

352
00:26:21,288 --> 00:26:23,372
Why have you fabricated stories

353
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:25,458
claiming that I sent gifts to you?

354
00:26:25,459 --> 00:26:26,668
What is your motivation?

355
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:29,045
They're not fabricated.

356
00:26:29,046 --> 00:26:30,129
You know that it's true.

357
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:32,465
Did you really think
that I would play along with this?

358
00:26:32,466 --> 00:26:34,760
Rashta didn't lie
about the necklace, though.

359
00:26:35,385 --> 00:26:38,430
Perhaps you have forgotten,
you sent it to me as a welcome present

360
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:40,223
for becoming mistress.

361
00:26:40,224 --> 00:26:41,849
What's all this?

362
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:43,393
Your Majesty.

363
00:26:45,521 --> 00:26:47,815
I'm only asking
about the rumors I've heard.

364
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:51,734
In this instance, a pearl necklace
that was not a gift from me.

365
00:26:51,735 --> 00:26:53,277
Did you ask Rashta personally?

366
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:54,822
Who else should I ask, Your Majesty?

367
00:26:56,115 --> 00:26:58,783
It would be easier to merely let it pass.

368
00:26:58,784 --> 00:27:01,285
No, I'm not willing to let it pass.

369
00:27:01,286 --> 00:27:02,830
My name is being misused.

370
00:27:03,497 --> 00:27:05,123
Majesty, it wasn't me.

371
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:06,875
I… I didn't lie.

372
00:27:08,710 --> 00:27:10,795
Do not question Rashta further.

373
00:27:10,796 --> 00:27:11,879
It is my doing.

374
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:14,466
I was the one who sent the gift
to Rashta in your name.

375
00:27:15,592 --> 00:27:18,428
Your Majesty… you sent it?

376
00:27:19,304 --> 00:27:21,390
If this really is your doing,

377
00:27:21,890 --> 00:27:23,934
may I ask Your Majesty's intentions then?

378
00:27:25,561 --> 00:27:27,562
Even if you are an emperor,

379
00:27:27,563 --> 00:27:30,691
you must not use another person's name
falsely as you please.

380
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:32,901
Is that not so?

381
00:27:33,402 --> 00:27:34,736
Your Majesty?

382
00:27:38,282 --> 00:27:40,575
Do you really have to ask
these questions now?

383
00:27:40,576 --> 00:27:41,743
Yes.

384
00:27:42,494 --> 00:27:44,495
I must hold you to account

385
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:45,747
because you have confessed.

386
00:27:49,251 --> 00:27:50,460
I'd like you to apologize now.

387
00:27:51,211 --> 00:27:52,295
You'd like what?

388
00:27:52,296 --> 00:27:54,464
I have been used quite unjustly.

389
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:56,174
Is that so hard?

390
00:28:08,061 --> 00:28:09,438
I apologize, then.

391
00:28:11,857 --> 00:28:14,526
What you said
made Rashta start spreading rumors.

392
00:28:15,027 --> 00:28:16,819
Your Majesty is accountable too.

393
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:18,780
You should correct this false information.

394
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:21,324
Are you serious?

395
00:28:21,325 --> 00:28:23,744
Are you worried
that it could hurt your dignity?

396
00:28:24,745 --> 00:28:27,038
No matter the damage you've caused to me.

397
00:28:27,039 --> 00:28:30,042
If a necklace of pearls
leaves your dignity damaged,

398
00:28:30,751 --> 00:28:33,295
then it must be as brittle
as a foundation of ice.

399
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:35,296
That could be.

400
00:28:35,297 --> 00:28:37,632
Even if that is so,
it does not acquit you,

401
00:28:37,633 --> 00:28:40,551
because correcting this
should be just as trivial.

402
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:43,638
I'm asking you.
Please do this with no more delay.

403
00:28:43,639 --> 00:28:46,474
This was something
you should have done, Navier.

404
00:28:46,475 --> 00:28:48,851
Is making a gesture with your name
so distasteful?

405
00:28:48,852 --> 00:28:50,604
Yes.

406
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:53,899
How very narrow-minded.

407
00:28:54,650 --> 00:28:55,733
You have changed.

408
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:57,611
Now you have heard my case.

409
00:29:01,782 --> 00:29:03,951
Give me my due respect…

410
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:06,078
Sovieshu.

411
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:29,934
Majesty, I'm all right,
so there's nothing to worry about now.

412
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:31,019
Let's go.

413
00:29:33,689 --> 00:29:34,731
I'm feeling tired.

414
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,234
You go on your own.

415
00:29:58,005 --> 00:29:59,714
Hmm?

416
00:29:59,715 --> 00:30:00,882
Let's go.

417
00:30:01,550 --> 00:30:03,092
What has just happened?

418
00:30:03,093 --> 00:30:05,177
It sounded
like a real ruckus in there earlier.

419
00:30:05,178 --> 00:30:07,513
You didn't cause any trouble,
did you, Your Highness?

420
00:30:07,514 --> 00:30:08,806
No, not me. Sovieshu.

421
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:10,266
- Sovieshu?
- Sovieshu.

422
00:30:10,267 --> 00:30:11,476
- Sovieshu.
- Tsk, tsk, tsk.

423
00:30:20,986 --> 00:30:22,195
Ah!

424
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:24,947
I was so busy
preparing for your party

425
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,949
that I was unable to visit
the palace this week.

426
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:28,868
Good heavens!

427
00:30:28,869 --> 00:30:30,661
So you went and caused trouble?

428
00:30:30,662 --> 00:30:31,829
Why on earth did you do it?

429
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:33,956
But it was for my party.

430
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:36,417
I was scared no one would come
and it would all be ruined.

431
00:30:38,045 --> 00:30:40,172
If it hadn't been for that Prince Heinrey…

432
00:30:41,590 --> 00:30:43,175
Should we still hold our event?

433
00:30:44,384 --> 00:30:45,385
Cancel it.

434
00:30:46,094 --> 00:30:48,512
Donate the food and gifts
we bought for it in Rashta's name

435
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:49,847
to the new home for orphans.

436
00:30:49,848 --> 00:30:51,182
And Ms. Rashta,

437
00:30:51,183 --> 00:30:53,059
the party's over for you this time.

438
00:30:53,060 --> 00:30:55,479
Banquets, outings, and games
are all paused.

439
00:30:56,313 --> 00:30:57,855
You will stay in seclusion!

440
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:58,981
Oh no!

441
00:30:58,982 --> 00:31:00,066
Not that!

442
00:31:01,485 --> 00:31:04,863
If anyone here is allowed to be upset,
it should be me and not you, girl!

443
00:31:07,074 --> 00:31:11,411
You will not survive in high society
if you're known for lying to people.

444
00:31:12,037 --> 00:31:13,370
Luckily for you,

445
00:31:13,371 --> 00:31:16,248
I will start the hard work needed
to renew your image,

446
00:31:16,249 --> 00:31:17,750
with the aid of our allies.

447
00:31:17,751 --> 00:31:19,919
Meanwhile, hold onto His Majesty's heart…

448
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:22,380
since it must not slip away.

449
00:31:23,715 --> 00:31:26,634
Do you know
who the most fickle person here is

450
00:31:26,635 --> 00:31:27,636
in this kingdom?

451
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:29,386
It's Sovieshu.

452
00:31:29,387 --> 00:31:32,098
That family's been fickle for generations.

453
00:31:32,099 --> 00:31:34,391
Their bloodline is all the same.

454
00:31:34,392 --> 00:31:37,561
Changeable as a weathervane
blown about by the breeze.

455
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:39,106
And insatiable too.

456
00:31:40,107 --> 00:31:41,690
All those heads…

457
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:45,069
parted so easily from their bodies
under the old king.

458
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,780
So many died.

459
00:31:47,322 --> 00:31:48,573
But why were they killed?

460
00:31:49,032 --> 00:31:50,033
Were they guilty?

461
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:56,206
Listen to me.

462
00:31:56,748 --> 00:31:58,959
Just one person can save you
from all this.

463
00:31:59,876 --> 00:32:01,128
I'm that person.

464
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:05,214
RASHTA ISHKA BOTULIN
BANQUET NOTICE

465
00:32:05,215 --> 00:32:06,298
CANCELLED

466
00:32:09,094 --> 00:32:10,177
RASHTA ISHKA BOTULIN

467
00:32:10,178 --> 00:32:12,096
TREASURE HUNT EVENT

468
00:32:12,097 --> 00:32:13,890
FIND THE WAY AND CLAIM THE TREASURE!

469
00:32:20,355 --> 00:32:22,983
Maid Annie was the perpetrator,
Your Majesty.

470
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:27,320
A pity.

471
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:30,448
I expect she gave in
because of her father's debts.

472
00:32:31,241 --> 00:32:32,701
You already suspected?

473
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:34,995
At the start,

474
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:38,832
I only shared it
because it was an amusing story.

475
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:42,085
But when they gave me money for it…

476
00:32:42,836 --> 00:32:45,004
that's when I started to think

477
00:32:45,005 --> 00:32:47,090
that what I had done was bad.

478
00:32:52,929 --> 00:32:55,390
Her Majesty is giving you this
for you to move away.

479
00:32:57,893 --> 00:32:59,351
You cannot be here.

480
00:32:59,352 --> 00:33:00,769
Hide from your father.

481
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:02,688
Take your son and live quietly.

482
00:33:05,859 --> 00:33:08,319
 The treasure lies
where fire and water meet,

483
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:10,196
and there stands a lighthouse.

484
00:33:10,197 --> 00:33:12,281
Find and bring back the two eyes

485
00:33:12,282 --> 00:33:14,618
that shine upon the world
from that lighthouse.

486
00:33:23,251 --> 00:33:25,669
Those of you
who picked the same animal,

487
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:27,380
please pair up together.

488
00:33:36,097 --> 00:33:37,681
It's a dragon.

489
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:40,184
Uh, who's got a dragon?

490
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:41,853
Dragon over here!

491
00:33:42,812 --> 00:33:45,315
- Who could it be?
-  Maybe no one else has one.

492
00:33:58,912 --> 00:34:00,997
I heard you have the dragon?

493
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:04,751
You too?

494
00:34:13,510 --> 00:34:15,344
If everyone
has found their partner,

495
00:34:15,345 --> 00:34:16,679
I declare the treasure hunt…

496
00:34:16,680 --> 00:34:17,846
Open!

497
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:24,688
I think Circe's a wonderful person.

498
00:34:27,899 --> 00:34:30,609
I'm afraid
she has a difficult journey ahead.

499
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:32,779
She will be inheriting
her country's throne.

500
00:34:34,531 --> 00:34:37,826
Your Majesty, you know everything
that's going on in the world.

501
00:34:39,869 --> 00:34:41,329
Shall we gallop as well?

502
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:46,458
Hyah!

503
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:21,953
My scarf blew off in the wind.

504
00:35:28,710 --> 00:35:29,961
Use this to secure it.

505
00:35:34,424 --> 00:35:35,800
It's one of Queen's feathers.

506
00:35:36,551 --> 00:35:37,677
It has so many uses.

507
00:35:38,595 --> 00:35:40,346
It works for sewing too.

508
00:35:40,347 --> 00:35:41,973
But also as a weapon.

509
00:35:43,350 --> 00:35:44,559
And a quill for letters.

510
00:35:47,312 --> 00:35:49,147
When you heard I was writing to you,

511
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:51,441
I hope you weren't disappointed.

512
00:35:56,154 --> 00:35:57,656
I was overjoyed.

513
00:36:00,116 --> 00:36:02,118
Your Majesty, I'm so glad it was you.

514
00:36:03,578 --> 00:36:04,746
I really mean it.

515
00:36:07,582 --> 00:36:08,833
How did you know…

516
00:36:10,043 --> 00:36:11,378
How did you know I was the one?

517
00:36:12,629 --> 00:36:15,089
Now we shall be friends
outside of the letters.

518
00:36:15,090 --> 00:36:17,966
So please, do not be a stranger,
since I…

519
00:36:17,967 --> 00:36:19,427
…found you at last.

520
00:36:20,595 --> 00:36:21,888
Hmm.

521
00:36:23,723 --> 00:36:25,975
You speak of friendship
outside the letters.

522
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:28,770
That would not be easy.

523
00:36:30,021 --> 00:36:31,856
I fear troublesome eyes would soon follow.

524
00:36:32,816 --> 00:36:34,818
It's a secret between us two.

525
00:36:41,157 --> 00:36:42,951
For how long have you known…

526
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:45,662
that I was the one writing to you?

527
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:47,747
Hmm…

528
00:36:48,331 --> 00:36:49,833
From when I first met you.

529
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:51,960
From that moment?

530
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:55,547
You mean when I welcomed you?

531
00:36:56,339 --> 00:36:57,424
For that long?

532
00:36:58,007 --> 00:37:00,135
When I spotted your smiling face…

533
00:37:01,010 --> 00:37:02,429
I just knew it.

534
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:09,602
Were you hungry?

535
00:37:10,603 --> 00:37:11,896
Was that nice?

536
00:37:17,152 --> 00:37:18,194
It's all right.

537
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:44,763
<i>Come to think of it,
Prince Heinrey…</i>

538
00:37:45,889 --> 00:37:47,557
<i>He has eyes as purple as yours.</i>

539
00:37:48,141 --> 00:37:50,185
I'm already enamored by it.

540
00:38:12,749 --> 00:38:14,501
If you don't stop looking at me,

541
00:38:15,043 --> 00:38:16,127
I think my heart will burst.

542
00:38:16,878 --> 00:38:17,879
Uh…

543
00:38:22,926 --> 00:38:24,469
You know, you resemble Queen.

544
00:38:26,137 --> 00:38:29,181
He is handsome.
It's only natural.

545
00:38:29,182 --> 00:38:30,934
He's so intelligent.

546
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:32,851
Very perceptive too.

547
00:38:32,852 --> 00:38:35,063
It's like we've always known each other.

548
00:38:35,605 --> 00:38:37,064
He truly understands…

549
00:38:37,065 --> 00:38:39,025
almost as though we're one.

550
00:38:41,277 --> 00:38:43,988
I never knew a bird
could have all those expressions.

551
00:38:44,614 --> 00:38:46,658
It sounds as though
you might be falling for him.

552
00:38:47,492 --> 00:38:49,660
If we were the same species…

553
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:51,871
Hmm, we would be quite good together.

554
00:38:54,374 --> 00:38:55,833
Ah, tell me…

555
00:38:55,834 --> 00:38:58,627
Whenever I stroke his derriere,

556
00:38:58,628 --> 00:39:01,172
he wiggles
and he lifts his bottom up like this.

557
00:39:01,756 --> 00:39:03,131
That must have some meaning?

558
00:39:03,132 --> 00:39:04,384
Ah…

559
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:06,553
Mmm…

560
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:10,055
It means "thank you," I'm certain.

561
00:39:10,056 --> 00:39:12,683
He's, uh, expressing his gratitude to you.

562
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:14,394
Ah, is that so?

563
00:39:15,770 --> 00:39:17,355
I must do it as often as I can.

564
00:39:21,067 --> 00:39:22,569
We're nearly there, I believe.

565
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:24,696
Will the treasure be here?

566
00:39:25,321 --> 00:39:26,906
Maybe at the end of this path?

567
00:39:53,683 --> 00:39:55,685
You said you wished to fly the skies.

568
00:39:57,353 --> 00:40:01,023
You once wrote that you wanted to soar
through the clouds like a bird.

569
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:03,776
Now you can fly
just like the bird you're in love with.

570
00:40:06,571 --> 00:40:09,407
And this was the true reason
that I had to find you.

571
00:40:10,325 --> 00:40:13,036
I'll show you the world
as Queen perceives it.

572
00:40:16,998 --> 00:40:18,291
Are you ready?

573
00:40:23,254 --> 00:40:24,505
- Hello.
-  Now?

574
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:31,971
Ready. Do it now. The sky.

575
00:40:35,099 --> 00:40:36,183
Welcome aboard.

576
00:40:36,184 --> 00:40:38,268
We are about to leave.

577
00:40:38,269 --> 00:40:40,104
Please mind the raised edge.

578
00:40:41,064 --> 00:40:42,940
And you, Your Highness,

579
00:40:42,941 --> 00:40:44,524
you mind yourself as well.

580
00:40:49,948 --> 00:40:52,492
Let's give it a go, huh? Let's do it.

581
00:40:56,621 --> 00:40:57,705
So long, then.

582
00:40:58,206 --> 00:40:59,748
Yes, yes, yes. Ah, hold on!

583
00:40:59,749 --> 00:41:01,249
Wait there!

584
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:03,251
Wait!

585
00:41:03,252 --> 00:41:05,379
- Your picnic! Your lunch!
- No, it's fine.

586
00:41:05,380 --> 00:41:07,548
Don't you want…

587
00:41:10,927 --> 00:41:12,971
Go on, go on. Now.

588
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:33,408
May I look yet?

589
00:41:34,951 --> 00:41:36,285
Just wait another minute.

590
00:41:48,006 --> 00:41:50,674
Now, when your eyes open,

591
00:41:50,675 --> 00:41:53,427
all those matters which are tormenting you

592
00:41:53,428 --> 00:41:56,139
will feel utterly trivial
and insignificant.

593
00:41:58,683 --> 00:41:59,892
Would you like to look?

594
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:02,437
Yes.

595
00:42:35,303 --> 00:42:36,429
What do you think?

596
00:42:37,638 --> 00:42:39,264
You may shout if you want to.

597
00:42:39,265 --> 00:42:40,808
Nobody can hear you up here.

598
00:42:52,904 --> 00:42:53,905
Now louder.

599
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:25,645
You should know…

600
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:29,982
your messages brought such comfort.

601
00:43:33,528 --> 00:43:35,488
I was so thrilled that it was you.

602
00:43:41,994 --> 00:43:43,496
I'm so grateful.

603
00:44:09,230 --> 00:44:11,565
The closing declaration
of the New Year's Ceremony

604
00:44:11,566 --> 00:44:12,567
will now be made.

605
00:44:27,290 --> 00:44:29,457
Thank you for allowing me this honor.

606
00:44:29,458 --> 00:44:30,877
I'm proud to speak.

607
00:44:38,301 --> 00:44:40,802
How marvelous our festivities were.

608
00:44:40,803 --> 00:44:43,096
What did you enjoy the most this year?

609
00:44:43,097 --> 00:44:45,891
I liked
Her Majesty Empress Navier the most!

610
00:44:45,892 --> 00:44:47,059
How very kind.

611
00:44:52,023 --> 00:44:55,568
And what did I enjoy the most
about the ceremony this New Year?

612
00:44:56,485 --> 00:44:59,155
The smiles and happy faces
I saw everywhere.

613
00:44:59,739 --> 00:45:01,240
We were once enemies.

614
00:45:01,741 --> 00:45:02,824
But today,

615
00:45:02,825 --> 00:45:06,454
we are holding one another's hands,
and we are joyous.

616
00:45:07,163 --> 00:45:09,915
We danced together
and sang together as well.

617
00:45:09,916 --> 00:45:11,082
Did we not?

618
00:45:11,083 --> 00:45:12,584
Hear, hear.

619
00:45:12,585 --> 00:45:14,378
The war has ended, but…

620
00:45:15,504 --> 00:45:18,799
its aftereffects linger over our people.

621
00:45:19,759 --> 00:45:23,845
So the time has come for us
to take up a new sacred fight.

622
00:45:23,846 --> 00:45:25,180
To feed the hungry,

623
00:45:25,181 --> 00:45:27,433
to clothe the poor and in need,

624
00:45:27,934 --> 00:45:30,102
and to teach our children to do better.

625
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:32,021
I have faith in us.

626
00:45:33,272 --> 00:45:35,107
And I need you to remember this.

627
00:45:36,192 --> 00:45:39,319
That when we sheath our weapons,
we are empowered.

628
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:42,198
Our hands become free
to reach out and help others.

629
00:45:42,823 --> 00:45:44,408
Let's make that our pledge…

630
00:45:45,034 --> 00:45:46,077
together.

631
00:45:46,744 --> 00:45:48,746
And may that light shine on.

632
00:45:51,791 --> 00:45:53,959
I declare, my dear friends…

633
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:55,294
the ceremony closed.

634
00:46:15,982 --> 00:46:18,234
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS
